{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And the anger of HaShem burned</b>: the meaning is that the wrath smoldered in them — for they are the class of the [divine] attribute of <b>anger</b> — <b>and He went</b> in order that the anger might do what it had been authorized to do. And although at the bush Scripture said (Exodus 4:14) ״וַיִּחַר אַף ה׳ בְּמֹשֶׁה״, there He marked out the measure that the anger would act upon him, namely that the power of the soul, which is the aspect of priesthood, would be removed from him and given to Aaron, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Zevaḥim 102a; Shemot Rabbah ch. 3) — for the impression there was the removal of priesthood. But here the anger executed a great judgment, for tzara'at is like death, as stated in the matter [of our Sages]; and in both of them the punishment was as His saying <b>in them</b>. And thus our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Sifrei): ״וַיִּפֶן״ etc. — He turned away from his tzara'at; except that Miriam was not healed immediately and at once as Aaron [was], and no person knew of his tzara'at."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:08.680055724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}